   All 12 measured control/theme pairs clear ≥3:1 against both the fill and
   the card comfortably (min 5.15:1, dark, vs input fill — above the
   ≈4.7:1 estimate in the task background because the measured stone-700
   fill rgb(68,64,60) and indigo-300 ring rgb(165,180,252) give a slightly
   higher ratio than the estimate; still a clear pass).

   Note on the accounts textarea specifically: its class list includes
   Tailwind `focus:ring-accent focus:border-accent` with NO `ring-{width}`
   utility present, so no competing `box-shadow` is generated by Tailwind
   (a bare `ring-{color}` utility only sets the `--tw-ring-color` custom
   property; it does not itself declare `box-shadow`). Measured computed
   `box-shadow` on the textarea is exactly the styles.css value in both
   themes, confirming the new `textarea:focus` rule is what's rendering,
   not silently overridden by Tailwind's ring utility.

   Pixel cross-check: `page.$('#dashboard-date-start').screenshot()` for
   both themes (focus-light-date.png, focus-dark-date.png — both visually
   show a clear ring), then PIL pixel sampling at the crop border:
   light `(1,1)=(79,70,229)`, dark `(1,1)=(164,179,251)` and
   `(1,41)=(165,180,252)` — matches the computed-style colours (dark's
   1px variance is antialiasing).

